  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q06 (plasma bracket on a Tormach 1300PL), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release; reproduced by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\nBracket 200 x 120 x 6 mild steel: Ø40 hole, two 12 x 30 slots, four Ø10 holes. Plasma Profile, holes first, outer last. `verify` answers:\n\n```\n\"findings\": [],\n\"gate\": {\"ok\": true, \"problems\": [],\n  \"not_judged\": \"stock sim did not judge this program: the 3D stock sim does not run for plasma - BracketPlasma judged by the 2D plasma laws (cut order, cut crossing, kerf crossing, tip-up): 4 warning(s) - BracketPlasma: plasma tip-up: the rapid into contour C2 crosses the slug of hole C1, already cut free near (81.84, -36.43) mm; ... the rapid into contour C4 crosses the slug of hole C2 ...; ... C5 crosses the slug of hole C2 ...; ... C7 crosses the slug of hole C6 ...\"},\n\"held_by\": [], \"ok\": true,\n\"operations\": [{\"name\": \"BracketPlasma\", \"status\": \"ok\", \"warnings\": []}]\n```\n\nThe plasma laws did judge the program and found 4 tip-up crossings (the torch rapids over slugs that are already cut free and may have tipped up), but the only place they appear is a sentence inside `not_judged`. A client reading `findings`, the operation's `warnings` or `ok` (the UI's verdict, an agent, a script) sees a clean program. The posted program keeps the crossings.\n\n## Expected\n\nEach tip-up crossing is a finding (with `blocks_post` as the law decides) and an operation warning, like the other laws' results; `not_judged` only says what was not judged. Better still, the cut order or the rapid route avoids crossing freed slugs (C2 is crossed twice).\n\n## Repro files\n\n[q06-bracket.camproj](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q06-wire-plasma/q06-bracket.camproj) (`open_project`, `generate`, `verify`), [q06-bracket.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q06-wire-plasma/q06-bracket.step), [q06-bracket.nc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q06-wire-plasma/q06-bracket.nc); agent report [REPORT.md](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q06-wire-plasma/REPORT.md) problem 16.\n\nDone means: verify on this project lists the 4 tip-up crossings in `findings` and in BracketPlasma's `warnings` (pinned by a test), and `ok`/`held_by` follow whatever blocking rule the tip-up law states.\n",
